@startuml eviction-pipeline
' ============================================================================
' Node-eviction pipeline — memory pressure → queued request → async eviction
' thread → epoch-quiescence wait → LRU cold-node select → atomic unswizzle.
'
' Source of truth:
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/memory_monitor.rs  (MemoryPressureMonitor;
'     Normal >30% / Low 10–30% / Critical <10% available, debounced),
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/eviction/coordinator.rs  (request_eviction maps
'     the pressure LEVEL → EvictionUrgency, the eviction_loop: cooldown →
'     wait_for_quiescence → perform_eviction → record stats),
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/eviction/disk_registry.rs  (select_for_eviction:
'     filter depth ≥ min_eviction_depth, score by LRU coldness, take coldest),
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/eviction/lru_tracker.rs   (coldness scoring), and
'   src/persistent_artrie/core/swizzled_ptr.rs           (unswizzle = the swap).
'   Level→urgency map (coordinator.rs):  Normal ⇒ no-op · Low ⇒ Moderate ·
'   Critical ⇒ Emergency.  Urgency scales batch_size (×1/×2/×4).
'
' Rendered as a FLAT state machine (no composite-state wrappers): PlantUML is
' robust for flat colored states + colored cross edges, whereas composite states
' with cross-boundary edges to colored top-level states mis-parse here. The five
' pipeline stages are marked by the comment banners below.
'
' Color key (urgency by severity, amber → red):
'   green (#C8E6C9) = Normal pressure — full caching, eviction idle
'   amber (#FFE0B2) = Low pressure / Moderate urgency — proactive eviction
'   red   (#FFCDD2) = Critical pressure / Emergency urgency — evict aggressively
'   grey  (#ECEFF1) = coordinator plumbing (queue, async thread, stats)
'   blue  (#BBDEFB) = the durable on-disk outcome (cold node is now a DiskRef)
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 24
hide empty description
skinparam StateBorderColor #37474F
skinparam StateFontName "DejaVu Sans"

title Eviction pipeline — pressure → urgency → LRU select → unswizzle

' ===== Stage 1: memory-pressure bands (MemoryPressureMonitor) =====
state "Normal\n>30% free\n(full cache)" as Normal #C8E6C9
state "Low\n10–30% free" as Low #FFE0B2
state "Critical\n<10% free" as Critical #FFCDD2

[*] --> Normal
Normal --> Low : avail < low
Low --> Critical : avail < crit
Critical --> Low : recovers
Low --> Normal : recovers

' ===== Stage 2: pressure level → eviction urgency (request_eviction) =====
Normal --> Idle : no-op
state "Eviction idle" as Idle #C8E6C9
Low -[#EF6C00]-> Queue : ⇒ Moderate
Critical -[#C62828]-> Queue : ⇒ Emergency

' ===== Stage 3: coordinator request queue =====
state "Coordinator queue\nVecDeque<Request>" as Queue #ECEFF1 : higher urgency MERGES\nwith the pending request\n(no duplicate cycles)
Queue --> Cooldown : async thread polls\ntry_pop (≈100 ms)

' ===== Stage 4: the async eviction-thread loop =====
state "Cooldown check" as Cooldown #ECEFF1 : skip if too recent or\n> 5 s stale (record_skip)
state "Wait epoch\nquiescence" as Quiesce #FFE0B2 : advance() →\nwait_for_quiescence\n(EBR — see\nepoch-reclamation)
state "Select cold\nnodes (LRU)" as Select #FFE0B2 : select_for_eviction:\nkeep depth ≥\nmin_eviction_depth, score\nby LRU coldness, take\ncoldest up to batch_size\n× urgency
state "Atomic unswizzle\nChild → DiskRef" as Swap #FFE0B2 : callback CAS-swaps each\ncold node; root stays\nin memory (path non-empty)
state "Record stats" as Stats #ECEFF1 : nodes_evicted ·\nbytes_freed ·\neviction_cycles ·\nlast_duration_ms
state "Skip cycle" as Skip #ECEFF1 : no eviction this pass

Cooldown --> Quiesce : within cooldown
Cooldown --> Skip : too recent →\nrecord_skip
Quiesce --> Select : readers drained
Quiesce --> Skip : timeout
Select --> Swap : non-empty set
Select --> Skip : empty → (0,0)
Swap --> Stats : nodes_evicted,\nbytes_freed
Stats --> Idle : cycle complete
Skip --> Idle : await request
Idle --> Cooldown : next request

' ===== Stage 5: durable outcome =====
Swap -[#1565C0]-> Evicted : RAM reclaimed\nafter EBR free
state "Cold node on disk\n(DiskRef →\nblock_id + location)" as Evicted #BBDEFB : re-faulted on next\naccess (lazy load via\nBufferManager)

note bottom of Stats #ECEFF1
  The eviction thread NEVER blocks
  client inserts/lookups: it runs in
  the background, holds only a
  Weak<Coordinator>, and evicts only
  nodes whose disk image is current —
  a write invalidates the registry
  until the next checkpoint re-publishes.
end note

legend right
| Color | Urgency / severity |
|<#C8E6C9>| Normal — full caching, idle |
|<#FFE0B2>| Low → Moderate — proactive |
|<#FFCDD2>| Critical → Emergency — aggressive |
|<#ECEFF1>| coordinator plumbing |
|<#BBDEFB>| durable on-disk outcome |
endlegend
@enduml
